    "body": "Under transformers>=5.6 PretrainedConfig is itself a dataclass, and a subclass field declared with field(default_factory=...) is mishandled: it raises \"non-default argument follows default argument\" at class-definition time, and even past that the transformers constructor reports it as a missing required field. This made importing loongforge.models.foundation (which eagerly imports glm5_next) fail on the pinned transformers 5.12.1 stack.\r\n\r\nDefault vision_config and moe_layer_freq to None and materialize them in __post_init__ instead of using default_factory. Behavior is preserved: vision_config still becomes a fresh Glm5NextVisionConfig() per instance (and the dict path is kept), and moe_layer_freq is unconditionally derived from mlp_layer_types later in __post_init__ regardless of its initial value.\r\n\r\n## Change Summary\r\n\r\n- What changed?\r\n- Which issue or requirement does this address?\r\n- Which modules are affected?\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- [ ] I ran the relevant local checks.\r\n- [ ] I added or updated tests where appropriate.\r\n- [ ] I checked compatibility with existing APIs and configurations.\r\n\r\n## CI, GPU, and Image Impact\r\n\r\n- [ ] This change affects dependencies, Dockerfiles, patches, or runtime environments.\r\n- [ ] GPU validation is required. Suggested suite: `llm_vlm` / `embodied`.\r\n- [ ] A local candidate image should be built during GPU validation.\r\n- [ ] No GPU or image validation is required.\r\n\r\n## Reviewer Notes\r\n\r\nDescribe any known risks, rollout considerations, or follow-up work.\r\n",
    "changed_files": 1,
